-- title:
--   Kernel of Frobenius lies in V(L)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring in which $p$ is a non-zero-divisor, and let $k$ be a commutative ring of characteristic $p$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra such that the structure map $\mathcal O \to k$ is surjective with kernel exactly the ideal generated by $p$. Let $\mathcal R$ be a commutative $\mathcal O$-bialgebra which is flat as an $\mathcal O$-module, and write $A = k \otimes_{\mathcal O} \mathcal R$ for the base change, with the induced $k$-bialgebra structure. Consider the Dieudonné module $M =$ [`Deformation.DieudonneModule k p A`](def/Dieudonne_WittHomColimit.html#L234), the direct limit over $n$, along the shift maps `wittHomShiftLE`, of the additive subgroups `wittHom k p n A` of $\mathrm{W}_n(A)$ consisting of those truncated Witt vectors $x$ whose image under the comultiplication $A \to A \otimes_k A$, applied coefficientwise, equals the sum of the images of $x$ under the two inclusions $A \to A \otimes_k A$; its Frobenius and Verschiebung are the endomorphisms of $M$ induced levelwise by `TruncWitt.frobeniusFun` and `TruncWitt.verschiebung`. The assertion is: if $z \in M$ satisfies $Fz = 0$, then $z = Vy$ for some $y$ in the subgroup [`Deformation.fontaineHodge k p π`](def/Dieudonne_FontaineHodge.html#L272), where $\pi\colon \mathcal R \to A$ is the ring homomorphism $r \mapsto 1 \otimes r$; this subgroup consists of the classes $z' =$ `of k p A n x` of elements $x \in$ `wittHom k p n A`, for some $n$, whose underlying truncated Witt vector lies in `TruncWitt.fontaineKer p n π`.
--
--   This is the statement that the kernel of $F$ on the Dieudonné module of the special fibre is contained in $V(L)$, where $L$ is Fontaine's submodule attached to the flat $\mathcal O$-bialgebra $\mathcal R$; it is one of the consequences Fontaine draws from his membership criterion, and is the exactness input used in Conrad's length computations. Within the project it feeds the construction of the Honda system attached to $\mathcal R$ and the counting of the quotient of $M$ by the Verschiebung image together with the images of the $p$-power maps.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Deformation_DieudonneModule_exists_mem_fontaineHodge_verschiebung_eq_of_frobenius_eq_zero.lean

